survivors.claim:
D6's source-ban test applies the locked runtime-import regex per line (deviation #2), which lets a multi-line runtime `import {
 createServer,
} from 'vite'` escape the ban entirely — the guard D6 exists to provide has a hole for the most common prettier-wrapped import shape. The deviation is forced (the locked regex applied whole-file false-positives on watch.ts), so this is advisory: a follow-up should tighten the pattern (e.g. run pattern 1 whole-file after excluding `import type` statements, or bound `[^;]*?` to `[^;'"]*?`) rather than revert to per-line.

survivors.evidence:
Executed scratch repro (node, deleted after): whole-file P1 on src/server/watch.ts → true, match = "import path from 'node:path'
import type { FSWatcher, ViteDevServer } from 'vite'" (false positive, so the deviation is forced); per-line P1 on watch.ts → false; multi-line runtime import "import {
  createServer,
} from 'vite'
" → whole-file: true | per-line: false (escapes the shipped test's matchedPatterns).
